        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Heading" table:number-columns-spanned="4" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Notes</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="3"/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row table:style-name="rh0_6"><table:table-cell table:style-name="NoteWrap" table:number-columns-spanned="4" office:value-type="string"><text:p>1.  Each unit pays its fixed share of the total in four equal quarterly instalments, rounded to the nearest penny.</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="3"/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row table:style-name="rh0_6"><table:table-cell table:style-name="NoteWrap" table:number-columns-spanned="4" office:value-type="string"><text:p>2.  The reserve fund is held for future repairs to the road and gates and is not spent in this year.</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="3"/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row table:style-name="rh0_6"><table:table-cell table:style-name="NoteWrap" table:number-columns-spanned="4" office:value-type="string"><text:p>3.  The shares add up to 100%. Unit 4’s share is 8.5%, which is about £2,560 a year on this budget.</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="3"/></table:table-row>
